          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There are several notions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            %em conjugate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConjugateTransformationOfAdjoints"}
            below).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            There are several layers of generality at which one may consider a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %em between
            adjoint functors.
          %p Here is a basic but important notion:
          %p
          #ConjugateTransformationOfAdjoints.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (conjugate transformations of adjoints)
              %br/
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of pairs of adjoint functors between the same
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            #eq:PairOfPairsOfAdjointFunctors.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %munderover
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ⊥
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi R
                                    %mn 1
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi L
                                    %mn 1
                            %mi 𝒟
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %munderover
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ⊥
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi R
                                    %mn 2
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi L
                                    %mn 2
                            %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R_1}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{L_1}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\;\;\; \bot \;\;\;}
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R_2}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{L_2}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\;\;\; \bot \;\;\;}
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    }
            %p
              then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              between the adjoints of the same chirality, of this form
            #eq:PairOfTransformations.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda \,\colon\, L_1 \to L_2
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\rho \,\colon\, R_2 \to R_1
                    \\,,
            %p
              is called
              %em conjugate for
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#MacLane71"}> MacLane (1971), §IV.7 (5)
              \&amp;rbrack; or a
              %em pseudo-transformation of
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#HarpazPrasma15"}> Harpaz &amp; Prasma (2015), Sec. 2.2
              \&amp;rbrack; the given adjunctions if they make the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commute
              %svg{:height => "93.906pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 284.79 93.906", :width => "284.79pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
