                    \\,.
            %p
          \&amp;lbrack;
          %a{:href => "#MacLane71"}> MacLane (1971), §IV.8 Thm. 2 &amp; Exc. 1 (p. 102)
          \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Therefore, from Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniqueConjugateMate"}
            and Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HorizontalCompositionOfConjugateTransformations"}
            we have:
          #CatAdj.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/very+large+category"}> very large
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+full+sub-2-category"} locally full sub-2-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CatAdj"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi adj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{adj}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            #eq:CatAdjInsideCat.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi adj
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cat_{adj} \longrightarrow Cat
            %p whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are categories,
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
                  which are conjugate in the sense of Def.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConjugateTransformationOfAdjoints"}
            %p
          \&amp;lbrack;
          %a{:href => "#MacLane71"}> MacLane (1971), §IV.8 below (1), p. 102
          \&amp;rbrack;
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_bifibrations Relation to bifibrations
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Under the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibrations"} Grothendieck fibrations
              which arise from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctors"} pseudofunctors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B} \longrightarrow Cat
              that factor through
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CatAdj"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi adj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{adj}
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CatAdjInsideCat"} (5)
              are equivalently the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibrations"} bifibrations
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              A Grothendieck construction on a pseudofunctor yielding a bifibration is fairly immediately equivalent to all base change functors having an adjoint on the respective side (e.g.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "bifibration#Jacobs98"} Jacobs (1998), Lem. 9.1.2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi adj
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{adj} \to Cat
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+full+sub-2-category"} locally full sub-2-category
              (Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniqueConjugateMate"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi adj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_adj
          See also
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#HarpazPrasma15"} Harpaz &amp; Prasma (2015), Prop. 2.2.1
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+transformation"} monad transformation
            %li
